{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03433",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.99,
      "end_seconds": 5.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Actually, hi doctor, am I too early?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.93,
      "end_seconds": 12.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "So, not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 12.87,
      "end_seconds": 22.13,
      "duration_seconds": 9.26,
      "text": "Let me think, um, morning, doctor. I'll stay and and fill in anything that's missed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.76,
      "end_seconds": 27.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.09,
      "end_seconds": 39.28,
      "duration_seconds": 10.19,
      "text": "oh, you know, mainly fever and shivers there's a couple of other things, but that's the main one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.92,
      "end_seconds": 43.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.94,
      "end_seconds": 48.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "I've, I've had it for two months"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.0,
      "end_seconds": 53.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.63,
      "end_seconds": 55.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Severe, really"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.52,
      "end_seconds": 61.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Has there been pain in the lower tummy too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.58,
      "end_seconds": 79.73,
      "duration_seconds": 16.15,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, that too. Right, as for pain in the lower tummy, moderate, really. It happens a few times a day. Oh, uh, and confusion."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.49,
      "end_seconds": 82.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "and cough, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.2,
      "end_seconds": 87.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "I haven't noticed any cough"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 88.07,
      "end_seconds": 94.57,
      "duration_seconds": 6.5,
      "text": "Actually, you know, doctor, I did notice cough. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.73,
      "end_seconds": 102.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.66,
      "text": "no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.38,
      "end_seconds": 114.63,
      "duration_seconds": 10.25,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Okay, a few quick ones: fall, vomiting or back pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.88,
      "end_seconds": 122.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "So, no, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.76,
      "end_seconds": 126.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "has your heart given you any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.25,
      "end_seconds": 130.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.51,
      "end_seconds": 140.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.78,
      "text": "are there any allergies I should be aware of? These questions might sound routine, but they matter"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.12,
      "end_seconds": 146.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Hmm, uh, no, I'm not allergic to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 148.41,
      "end_seconds": 155.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.97,
      "text": "I'm not sure that's right i seem to recall a problem with amoxicillin"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.44,
      "end_seconds": 160.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "I mean, I don't remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.79,
      "end_seconds": 167.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "okay, I'll note both of those. Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.81,
      "end_seconds": 172.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "I have an enlarged prostate. Yes, migraines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.74,
      "end_seconds": 176.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "I see, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.06,
      "end_seconds": 180.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "I, I have asthma"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.56,
      "end_seconds": 187.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.34,
      "end_seconds": 190.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "My grandfather had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.79,
      "end_seconds": 197.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.73,
      "end_seconds": 224.1,
      "duration_seconds": 24.37,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I gave up cigarettes last spring. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts. I live with my elderly mother. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.62,
      "end_seconds": 230.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 232.05,
      "end_seconds": 253.47,
      "duration_seconds": 21.42,
      "text": "so, he takes tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, at night. Actually, it's sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed for my migraines, doctor. I mean, he is on Foracort inhaler, twice a day, I give it to him"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.16,
      "end_seconds": 258.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 259.03,
      "end_seconds": 264.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "For two months. It's a urinary catheter, in place, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.99,
      "end_seconds": 275.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "so, I'll note down your vital signs first"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.27,
      "end_seconds": 291.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "That's it, just a a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.37,
      "end_seconds": 320.55,
      "duration_seconds": 10.18,
      "text": "Okay: temp 38.3 degrees, heart rate 88, oxygen saturation is 95 percent, blood pressure 117 over 79, respiratory rate 17."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.74,
      "end_seconds": 323.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.24,
      "end_seconds": 328.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.77,
      "end_seconds": 335.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.29,
      "end_seconds": 353.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.79,
      "end_seconds": 357.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.13,
      "end_seconds": 378.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "The catheter bag has cloudy urine and there is tenderness above the pubic bone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.85,
      "end_seconds": 386.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.66,
      "end_seconds": 401.55,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, it points towards a catheter-related urinary infection. We shouldn't forget urosepsis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.54,
      "end_seconds": 404.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 405.21,
      "end_seconds": 418.56,
      "duration_seconds": 13.35,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a catheter-related urinary infection, and we'll know more once the blood tests is back. I think blood tests makes sense here, for fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 422.47,
      "end_seconds": 425.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "ah, do I need to prepare?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 427.52,
      "end_seconds": 440.04,
      "duration_seconds": 12.52,
      "text": "I want a urine culture done, that's for possible urinary infection. Change the catheter and drink plenty. We'll catch up in two days. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 441.66,
      "end_seconds": 444.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks"
    }
  ]
}